From 0b1f8bb3a1af8257fc1bce628f159d4cf03c0ead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slice-runners lane <lane@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:13:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(refinement): runner premises for call-free bytecode

StaticRunner and OutputRunner are refuted at gas 2^255 (IDENTITY returns its
call data, so a message with 2^256 bytes of data ends with an output of that
size). For bytecode whose linear decode has no CREATE, CALL, CALLCODE,
DELEGATECALL, CREATE2, STATICCALL, RETURNDATASIZE or RETURNDATACOPY
(callFree), checkCB/checkXB acceptance gives checkC/checkX acceptance with the
call flag cleared, so the final theorems need no runner hypothesis.
CalleesRun is discharged for bytecode with no 0xfa byte.
